<article class="env-lemma" id="0835">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0835">Lemma <span data-tag="0835">67.17.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subspace. If $U \to X$ is quasi-compact, then $U$ is scheme theoretically dense in $X$ if and only if the scheme theoretic closure of $U$ in $X$ is $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/082Z" data-tag="082Z">67.16.3</a> part (3). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>